{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q22808799","formula":"C₁₄H₂₁NOS","hill":"C14H21NOS","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Prosulfocarb"},"descriptions":{"en":"Prosulfocarb is a preëmergent herbicide used agriculturally in Australia, the EU, Japan, New Zealand, (since 2020), Morocco and Iran, for control of annual ryegrass and toad rush in wheat and barley crops. It was introduced to the EU in 1988 and is rapidly growing in use, with sales increasing by over 500% in France since 2008. Prosulfocarb is a thiocarbamate, and is absorbed by the roots of germinating seedlings to inhibit growth in the meristem by inhibiting fat synthesis, of resistance HRAC Group J, (Aus), Group N, (WSSA), Group 8."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":62020,"mass":251.39,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCN(CCC)C(=O)SCC1=CC=CC=C1","inchikey":"NQLVQOSNDJXLKG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"S-benzyl N,N-dipropylcarbamothioate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"62020","atoms":38,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.204,"y":0.186,"z":0.103,"el":"S"},{"x":1.237,"y":-1.725,"z":-0.941,"el":"O"},{"x":2.489,"y":0.036,"z":-0.079,"el":"N"},{"x":3.797,"y":-0.505,"z":-0.429,"el":"C"},{"x":2.518,"y":1.332,"z":0.601,"el":"C"},{"x":4.381,"y":-1.375,"z":0.677,"el":"C"},{"x":2.466,"y":2.501,"z":-0.376,"el":"C"},{"x":1.292,"y":-0.636,"z":-0.372,"el":"C"},{"x":5.756,"y":-1.927,"z":0.329,"el":"C"},{"x":2.517,"y":3.853,"z":0.322,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.442,"y":-1.007,"z":-0.452,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.844,"y":-0.546,"z":-0.163,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.525,"y":0.209,"z":-1.108,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.44,"y":-0.881,"z":1.046,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.825,"y":0.636,"z":-0.841,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.74,"y":-0.454,"z":1.313,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.433,"y":0.305,"z":0.37,"el":"C"},{"x":4.475,"y":0.318,"z":-0.683,"el"